      "message": "feat(tools): .camtools carries the tool body; \"Import tool holders\" toggle\n\nA tool library entry's definition may carry `body`, the ToolBodyDto a\n.camproj tool stores (drawn holder profile, placed mesh, lathe holder).\nAdditive: old files read unchanged and older builds ignore the key.\nExport writes it; the reader judges it as the project loader does\n(re-derived envelope, fitted to its tool) and refuses the file naming\nthe tool otherwise.\n\nThe import takes the holders choice as a parameter of the one undoable\nImportTools command (with_holders); the Tool library page gets an\n\"Import tool holders\" checkbox (default on, remembered per user in the\nprefs file) and MCP import_tool_library an optional `holders` flag.\nOff lands every tool bare. The identical-tool skip compares the body\nonly when one lands. camcraft-mcp skill doc updated; PROCESS_VERSION 17.\n\nFixes #889\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
